The mud supports the standard ANSI colors and attributes through color
tags.  You can insert these tags in any text you type such as SAY or TITLE
or even messages on the board or via notes.

These are of the format

   ##{<tag1> <tag2> ...}      (If you want to type a ## character type ####)

valid tags are as follows

   ##{off}           clears all previous tag state
   ##{bold}          #{bold}bold text#{off}
   ##{underline}     #{underline}underline text#{off}
   ##{flash}         #{flash}flashing text#{off}
   ##{reverse}       #{reverse}reverse text#{off}
   ##{black}         #{black}black#{off}
   ##{red}           #{red}red#{off}
   ##{green}         #{green}green#{off}
   ##{blue}          #{blue}blue#{off}
   ##{cyan}          #{cyan}cyan#{off}
   ##{magenta}       #{magenta}magenta#{off}
   ##{yellow}        #{yellow}yellow#{off}
   ##{white}         #{white}white#{off}
   ##{BLACK}         #{white BLACK}black background#{off}
   ##{RED}           #{white RED}red background#{off}
   ##{GREEN}         #{white GREEN}green background#{off}
   ##{BLUE}          #{white BLUE}blue background#{off}
   ##{CYAN}          #{CYAN}cyan background#{off}
   ##{MAGENTA}       #{MAGENTA}magenta background#{off}
   ##{YELLLOW}       #{YELLOW}yellow background#{off}
   ##{WHITE}         #{black WHITE}black background#{off}

As indicated you can do compound tags such as
   ##{red bold}This##{off} is an ##{bold under yellow flash BLUE}OBNOXIOUS##{off}##{blue}example##{off}

which would display the following text
    #{red bold}This#{off} is a #{bold under yellow flash BLUE}OBNOXIOUS#{off} example#

Make sure you end your text with \#{off} so it doesn't spell over to other lines.  

Please exercise restraint in using colors during play.  
If this is abused players will loose access to this feature.

Perhaps the most difficult part of making a new area is the file creation
process.  You need a mob file, an obj file, and a zone file.  Each of these
is detailed in their respective help entries.  (mob_file, obj_file, and
zone_file)

OBJ FILE FORMAT
---------------

Req'd?
(y/n)  Field name     Example Values        Description
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  y    name           { a short sword }     What it is and how it shows up
                      { Skullthumper }      in inventory/equipment lists.
                                            Capitalize proper nouns, others not
  y    namelist       { sword short }       A list of 'keywords' to refer to
                      { mace skull thumper }the object.  Try to include as many
                                            as you think will be tried.
  y    longdesc       { <see example> }     What you will see it as if it is
                                            sitting on the ground.  Note
                                            clothes should lie in a heap.
  n    action         { ? }                 Don't use this unless you know
                                            what it's for.
  n    weight         { 2 }                 The weight in pounds.  For weapons
                                            will determine how fast you can
                                            swing it.
  n    value          { 1000 }              The item's value in gold when
                                            bought or sold.  (Note - this will
                                            be totally different.)
  n    extras {
              keywords { note paper }
              desc { This is a note }       Extra fields which can be LOOKed
              }                             at.  Alternate between "keywords"
                                            and "desc" for multiple fields.
  n    flags          { glow, hum }         Flags which govern behavior of
                      { magic }             the item, or who can use it.
                                            See list below.
  y    wear           { finger }            A list of places where the object
                      { wield }             can be worn.  Please list only one
                                            unless there's a good reason.
  n    min_level      { 20 }                The minimum level which can use
                      { 90 }                this item.  If you are below the
                                            item, you can't use it!
  n    max_exist      { 1 }                 The maximum number of items which
                                            can exist at any time in the player
                                            file.  No max should be over 5. If
                                            you want to be totally realistic,
                                            there shouldn't be a max specified
                                            over 1.
  n    material       { wood }              Defines what the object is made of.
                                            Please specify only one.  See list
                                            below.
  n    apply {        strength { 2 }        A list of fields which take values,
                      immunity { xxxx }     which are then applied to the
             }                              player wearing the object. Be
                                            realistic, no +5 hit/dam boots.
  y    <type>         <varied>              Specify the item type here, as
                                            a seperate field, most take
                                            additional parameters.
------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

Lists
-----

Flags:
    Glow, Hum  --  Modifies how it looks to people
    Anti-good, Anti-evil, Anti-neutral  --  Doesn't let alignment wear
    Nodamage, Nodrop, Notake  --  ??
    Flexible, Mundane  --  ??
    Magic  --  Obviously a magic item, barbarians don't like it
    Invisible  --  Item cannot be seen (use sparingly)

Wear slots:
    Finger, neck, body, head, legs, feet, hands, arms, shield,
    waist, wrist, light, hold, wield, held, pouch, about

Materials:
    none, adamantium, aluminum, bone, brass, bronze, carbon,
    ceramic, cloth, copper, crystal, fur, gemstone, glass, gold,
    ice, iron, lead, leather, mithril, organic, paper, plastic,
    platinum, scale, silk, silver, steel, stone, tin, titanium,
    wax, wood, zinc, banded

Applies:
    strength, agility, intelligence, wisdom, endurance, mana, hp,
    move, all_ac, hitroll, damroll, save_paralysis, save_rod,
    save_petrification, save_breath, save_spell, save_all,
    backstab, kick, sneak, hide, bash, pick, steal, track,
    ac_feet, ac_legs, ac_arms, ac_body, ac_head,
    stopping_all, stopping_feet, stopping_legs, stopping_arms,
    stopping_body, stopping_head
        These all take integer parameters, and modify the player's
        statistic by that number (positive or negative)

    spell_affect   Various (useful?) affects (only one may be used):
    blink, invisible, detect-evil, detect-invisible, detect-magic,
    sense-life, sanctuary, flying, protect-evil, infravision,
    water-breath, sneak, hide, true-sight, fireshield, detect-evil,
    invulnerability, nosleep, nosummon, nocharm, haste, nofear

    weapon_spell_affect { spell }
        This will cast the given spell at the defender
        each time a hit is scored.  Only works on weapons.
        The spell will have an effective level of 6.

    eat_spell { spell }
        Only works on food/drink.  Spell goes off when item is
        eaten/drunk.

    immunity
    resistance
    susceptibility  Immunity bits are:
        fire, cold, electricity, energy, blunt, pierce,
        slash, acid, poison, drain, sleep, charm,
        hold, non-magical, plus 1, plus 2, plus 3, plus 4
    EX: immune { cold, energy, fire }

